# Walking: the one thing this game does with the wheel that a menu does not.
#
# `hold <side> [frames]` pins a finger to one side of the wheel, which is what holding one of the
# four Touch keys does. The game teaches this itself — it draws the wheel with its lower quarter
# lit and says TOUCH THE LOWER SIDE OF THE WHEEL TO MAKE JACK MOVE DOWNWARDS — and then answers
# EXCELLENT! when he does, which is the game confirming the direction rather than this project
# asserting it. The last screenshot is that moment.
#
# The five selects clear the opening dialogue; movement is refused until it is done.
#
# No screenshot is taken while the tutorial's wheel is on screen, and that is deliberate rather
# than convenient: that overlay is the one thing this project and the emulator disagree about
# (PLAN.md, the day's last entry), so a comparison there would be measuring a known open question
# instead of this feature.
440: select
480: wheel -24
520: select
620: select
760: select
1400: select
1500: select
1600: select
1700: select
1800: select
1950: hold bottom 200
2200: shot
2250: hold bottom 200
2500: shot
2520: quit
